      "plain": "\n █████    ███    ██   ██   stayAwakeBot\n██       █████   ██   ██   the sentinel saw the worm\n ████   ██   ██  ██ █ ██\n    ██  ███████  ███████   detect · report · auto-fix\n█████   ██   ██   ██ ██ \n\nWhat it is\n  A local supply-chain worm hunter — it detects, reports, and auto-fixes\n  self-propagating malware: obfuscated loaders, fake fonts, VS Code\n  auto-run tasks, and stealth \"evil merges\".\n\nThree verbs\n  saw scan   hunt worms (read-only) — the exit code IS the verdict\n  saw fix    recover from git onto a clean branch; --pr opens a PR\n  saw audit  credential · editor · CI hygiene\n\nWhy it's safe\n  · runs zero code at install (that's the very vector it hunts)\n  · fully accurate offline; only sandbox-escaping -x is opt-in\n  · persists nothing by default\n\nGate CI  saw scan  →  exit 1 on infection fails the build\nDocs     github.com/Ndevu12/stayAwakeBot\nsaw v0.6.2\n\n"
